113
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:49,000
Bungee gum contains the properties of both rubber and gum, you see.

114
00:08:49,000 --> 00:09:06,000
Catching the ball while the body is touching outside the court is illegal!

115
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:08,000
Razor is out!

116
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:12,000
Which means the winner of the match is Team Gon!

117
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:13,000
Oh my god!

118
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:14,000
Oh my god!

119
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:15,000
Nice!

120
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:17,000
Huh?

121
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:18,000
I missed it!

122
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:19,000
What happened at the very end?

123
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:23,000
Total defeat.

124
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:25,000
Really?

125
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:27,000
So then Hisuka clinched it for us!

126
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:30,000
Or he stole our glory, but that depends on how you look at it.

127
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:33,000
We won because we all worked together.

128
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:35,000
That makes this a team victory.

129
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:38,000
You sound so out of character, Hisuka.

130
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:40,000
I lose.

131
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:44,000
As I promised, we'll all leave this town immediately.

132
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:45,000
Oh.

133
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:46,000
Yeah.

134
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:48,000
Well, that is what we wanted.

135
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:49,000
But first...

136
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:53,000
You asked about Jean, so I'll tell you.

137
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:58,000
You were so reckless!

138
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:01,000
It's no wonder your hands are all destroyed!

139
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:02,000
Are you even listening?!

140
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:08,000
To answer your question, Jean is not here.

141
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:11,000
And I don't know where he is.

142
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:14,000
Right.

143
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:16,000
Well, I kind of expected that.

144
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:20,000
But, I can tell you some old stories if you like.

145
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:23,000
Sure!

146
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:27,000
I am a convict on death row.

147
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:30,000
You see, I've murdered people.

148
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:34,000
Caught and incarcerated, sentenced to death.

149
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:37,000
Then Jean hired me to come here.

150
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:39,000
He taught me something important.

151
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:43,000
That if one person in this entire world believes in you,

152
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:45,000
just one,

153
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:47,000
you can be redeemed.

154
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:50,000
One day, my son's going to come here.

155
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:53,000
When he does, don't hold back!

156
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:56,000
Fine. Does that mean that I can kill him?

157
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:57,000
Don't underestimate him.

158
00:10:57,000 --> 00:10:58,000
Don't underestimate him.

159
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:00,000
He is my kid.

160
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:03,000
I'm counting on you.

161
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:05,000
Thanks, Razor.

162
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:09,000
I always thought your dad was a little bit crazy.

163
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:11,000
Said he was making a game.

164
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:14,000
And the way he would talk about it for hours and hours on end

165
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:16,000
reminded me of an excited little kid or something.

166
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:21,000
Then he hired me, a condemned man, to fight his son.

167
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:23,000
You scum!

168
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:26,000
I hope you realize you owe me your life!

169
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:28,000
Hey!

170
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:29,000
You!

171
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:30,000
Over there!

172
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:31,000
What?

173
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:32,000
That thing?

174
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:34,000
I'm counting on you.

175
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:35,000
Thanks, Razor.

176
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:43,000
It felt like...

177
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:47,000
Like no one had ever called me by my name before.

178
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:51,000
Jean believed in your strength.

179
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:53,000
That's why he left you to me.

180
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:56,000
I believed in your strength too.

181
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:59,000
Which is why I didn't hold back.

182
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:01,000
Yeah.

183
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:04,000
But I couldn't have won without the help of everybody else.

184
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:06,000
That was great teamwork.

185
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:07,000
Yeah!

186
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:12,000
Now, go find Jean.

187
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:15,000
Okay!

188
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:30,000
Well, this is the place.

189
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:32,000
A window?

190
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:36,000
From this vantage point, we can see the shore.

191
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:40,000
So, how do we get to Poseidon's cavern from here?

192
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:52,000
Directly underneath that point, where the light shines.

193
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:54,000
You'll find an underground cavern.

194
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:56,000
But you won't find any treasure.

195
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:58,000
Because there isn't any.

196
00:12:58,000 --> 00:13:01,000
I feel terrible for deceiving all of you.

197
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:03,000
There's no treasure?

198
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:09,000
We consider the cavern to be sacred, so only a few fishermen know exactly where it's located.

199
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:15,000
All of the other stories you've heard were just rumors that took on a life of their own.

200
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:20,000
But Razor and his pirate friends simply wouldn't believe us.

201
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:28,000
Those who live off the bounty of the sea can never defile it.

202
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:34,000
Or that's what they said, right before they were buried with their secrets.

203
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:39,000
Hey, don't forget, okay? It's just a story in a video game.

204
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:45,000
I can finally see the ocean again from here.

205
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:48,000
The rising sun.

206
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:51,000
The boats returning with their hauls.

207
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:54,000
All the colors sparkling across the water.

208
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:59,000
If you ask me, this is the greatest treasure of them all.

209
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:10,000
Yes! We finally got the strip of beach cart. Let's use clone. We gotta make two copies.

210
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:13,000
We're fine taking the copies.

211
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:17,000
Of course. You deserve to take the original.

212
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:22,000
Are you sure you don't want anything, Heizuka?

213
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:25,000
No, I've had enough fun.

214
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:27,000
Hey, why don't you stick around and join us?

215
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:30,000
I want to know what the troop is up to.

216
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:34,000
Oh, I'm not interested in collecting cards.

217
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:37,000
But contact me if anything else comes up.

218
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:41,000
I'll cast a company or magnetic force to fly over.

219
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:48,000
Huh? That jerk, he lied to us!

220
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:53,000
Huh? We haven't used magnetic force at all since Heizuka teamed up with us, am I right?

221
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:55,000
Uh-huh.

222
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:59,000
That means when he ran into us that he already knew about spell cards, get it?

223
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:00,000
Huh?

224
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:08,000
Killua, there are some liars who only lie when there's a good reason to, and then there are those who will lie without any reason at all.

225
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:11,000
You and I are the former, but Heizuka's the latter.

226
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:14,000
And fretting won't get you anywhere. Accept it.

227
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:20,000
Attention! Another player has cast contact on you.

228
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:24,000
It's been a while. Do you know who this is?

229
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:26,000
Get through!

230
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:28,000
What do you want?

231
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:30,000
First, I'd like to congratulate you.

232
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:32,000
What do you mean?

233
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:34,000
Aw, don't play dumb.

234
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:35,000
Don't play dumb.

235
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:41,000
So here's the deal. I promise to spare your lives, and you hand over the strip of beach in return.

236
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:43,000
That's ridiculous.

237
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:48,000
Well, I must admit I am somewhat interested to see if you can beat us.

238
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:59,000
If you're willing to make a deal, then come alone to Masadora's entrance gate in one hour. If you don't, we'll take the card by force.

239
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:05,000
Oh, and don't bother running or trying to hide. We have a lot of accompanies.

240
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:11,000
How? I knew you'd find out, but I never thought it would be so soon.

241
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:19,000
Asta, Amana, Mannheim, Nickyuu, Suhail, Kazu.

242
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:23,000
They were all members of your party of fifteen, correct?

243
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:28,000
If you'll just check your binder, you'll notice that they're no longer with us.

244
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:30,000
What?!

245
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:35,000
This means they're either dead, or they're not in the game anymore.

246
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:41,000
Get through!

247
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:43,000
Who are you?

248
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:46,000
I'm Gon Freaks, and I'm ready to take you on!

249
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:51,000
Gon, huh? So you're one of those three brats.

250
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:54,000
I see you have wild luck Alexandrite.

251
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:59,000
I'll find you when I'm done with Tezgera, unless you want to give up the card now.

252
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:04,000
Get over here right now! I want to fight you! I also have own!

253
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:07,000
Tezgera, talk somewhere else!

254
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:14,000
Attention, another player has cast contact on you.

255
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:20,000
This is Finks. We found him. We're heading in your direction as we speak.

256
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:25,000
Wouldn't it be faster to target the kids?

257
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:29,000
They probably don't have the original strip of beach, but I bet they got a copy.

258
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:34,000
If so, it would be a card created by Clone.

259
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:36,000
Yeah, you're right.

260
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:41,000
Once those kids see Tezgera surrender, they'll give up without a fight.

261
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:47,000
If we target the brats, Tezgera will have time to recover, which could be rather troublesome.

262
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:53,000
He's a single Star Hunter, after all. And we don't know what his ability is.

263
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:57,000
Genthru doesn't know what you're capable of.

264
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:01,000
He and his team assume that we have the original strip of beach.

265
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:04,000
And that could prove to be very helpful.

266
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:07,000
So they're after what they think is the original card.

267
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:09,000
The one we have.

268
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:14,000
We'll buy you as much time as possible. Use it to regain your strength.

269
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:18,000
If you want to beat this game, you'll have no choice but to fight them.

270
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:23,000
You're the only ones with a chance of beating them. There's no doubt in my mind.

271
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:28,000
But Gon, what you did just now was selfish.

272
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:31,000
But more than that, it was incredibly foolish.

273
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:37,000
If they had accepted your challenge and come, what would have happened to Kilowoc given the extent of his injuries?

274
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:45,000
By losing control of your emotions, you endangered not only yourself, but your friends too.

275
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:48,000
I'm really sorry.

276
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:57,000
That aside, it will all come down to a company. If we can stave off their pursuit, we should be able to buy plenty of time.

277
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:04,000
But if we let too much time pass, then they might just decide to change things and target you instead.

278
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:08,000
We probably have a week, more, and you're on your own.

279
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:17,000
One week. That's not very long. And to be honest, it's probably optimistic. They might even decide to focus on us after only three days or so.

280
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:26,000
Then I'll team up with Tezgera. What about you? What are you gonna do? If we're buying you time, that implies we have an alliance.

281
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:35,000
Wait. There's very little benefit in allying with them. Especially now that the enemy knows that the eight of us have been working together.

282
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:41,000
And that being the case, we won't be able to act as decoys while you take out Genthru.

283
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:48,000
So of course, we'll have to be careful with the two cards they still lack. Both number two and number 75.

284
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:53,000
Leaving them with any one party would be dangerous and we can't afford the risk.

285
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:59,000
That means that my offer to buy time isn't an alliance. What I'm offering you is a trade.

286
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:01,000
A trade, huh?

287
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:11,000
Just three weeks. That's all the time we can buy you. And if we succeed, you'll give us number 75, the Wild Luck Alexandrite card.

288
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:15,000
I don't get it. You just said you can only buy us a week.

289
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:23,000
Well, that's assuming that we stay on the run for that long. If necessary, I may be able to force a stalemate of sorts.

290
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:29,000
Oh, I see. But if you guys really want 75, we'll just tell you how you can get your hands on it.

291
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:37,000
No. We're well aware of how to obtain it. Some of us only have a few empty slots left, and that's including Gorenu.

292
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:45,000
We would be required to turn all of our cards over to the villagers, and that's no longer reasonable. Three weeks.

293
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:54,000
But that isn't nearly enough time for Kilawa's hands to heal, or to close the gap between our abilities and those of Genthru.

294
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:58,000
So, we should use that time to come up with a workable strategy.

295
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:08,000
Yes, exactly. Devise a scenario that you can win. Identify the circumstances, and then prepare to carry out the strategy.

296
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:14,000
We got it!

297
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:24,000
Good. We'll leave now and delay Team Genthru all we can. And never forget, Goren. They've killed over 50 players in this game so far.

298
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:30,000
If you truly want to beat the game, you'll have to fight them.

299
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:35,000
Accompany on! To Masadora!

300
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:42,000
Just three weeks? That sure isn't very much time.

301
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:48,000
Kilawa, you focus on healing. While you're doing that, think of a strategy to help us beat Genthru.

302
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:55,000
Right. Goren, you'll train with me. If we can just get you to where you can avoid his little flower, we'll be in good shape.

303
00:21:56,000 --> 00:21:57,000
Us!

304
00:21:58,000 --> 00:22:04,000
Goren has won his match against Razor, but the Bombers are still far more powerful than his group of allies.

305
00:22:05,000 --> 00:22:07,000
Will they be able to find a path to success?

